    {"category":"COMMUNITY","family":"hill_footpath_lighting","source":"electric_cooperative_pole_maps_and_village_minutes","topic":"footpath safety lighting","story":"Residents on a steep path between the bus stop and clinic have asked for low-energy lamps and protective conduit at three bends.","support":"Village minutes identify the route and affected households. The electricity cooperative's pole map and installer quote match the three proposed locations.","fraud_story":"The campaign asks for lamps along the clinic route and attaches a village resolution plus an installer estimate.","fraud_docs":["Village resolution: lamps approved for the uphill clinic path at poles 14, 16, and 19.","Cooperative pole map: poles 14, 16, and 19 serve the industrial access road on the opposite ridge, not the clinic path."],"border_story":"Residents support improved lighting, but the utility has not confirmed whether the proposed bends can connect to a safe supply.","border_doc":"Site inspection requested; connection capacity and installation permissions are pending."},
